WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.999
Film Courage: Being the hot young writer,
being on the cover of Variety, your name is

00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:07.020
out there, and probably your phone is ringing
a lot.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.580
I know you’ve talked in other interview
about how some of this went away for a little

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.580
bit.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.520
Can you talk about how if someone else is
in a similar situation, how they regroup?

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:22.140
Corey Mandell: What I’d like to do is give
the single best piece of advice that is most

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.080
forgotten, that is ignored.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.699
And so what happened is when I was on the
front page of Variety and all these offers

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:35.819
were coming in, there was an agent at my agency
(Barbara Dreyfus), who didn’t represent

00:00:35.819 --> 00:00:40.120
me, but she took me out to lunch and she gave
me the following advice.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:46.749
She said “The next script you write is the
most important script you’ll ever write.

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:52.019
It will determine the trajectory of your career.

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:54.550
So right now you were an unknown person.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.270
You are on everyone’s radar.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:57.879
You worked with a high-profile director.

00:00:57.879 --> 00:01:00.510
He’s planning on making the movie.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.329
He said how great your script was.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:04.629
Everyone in town wants to work with you.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:06.960
Everyone is like so hyped up on you.”

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.130
Now there are like writers who are commodity
writers.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.423
They go in and they write these summer movies
and these big action movies and they make

00:01:16.423 --> 00:01:17.740
a lot of money.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:18.790
But there is nothing special about them.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.670
And then there are writers who are A-list
writers.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.289
Writers who have these amazing careers.

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:27.009
The next script you write will put you on
a trajectory.

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:33.780
So her advice was this…don’t take any
job you wouldn’t have done for free which

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.859
was to say you love this project and you believe
you can just knock it out of the park.

00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:40.630
You love this so much, you would do it without
getting paid.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.719
Now we’re going to get you paid but don’t
take anything that falls short of that.

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.670
Just say no to a lot of stuff because most
of what they are going to offer is crap or

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.570
just not a good fit for you.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.510
And the offers are going to start to slow
down and you are going to panic and think

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.790
you have to grab the next best one, don’t!

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:01.070
And the offers will keep slowing down and
I’m telling you this even…you’ll think

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.319
that the offers will eventually go away and
they won’t.

00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:09.440
But even if they do, literally you’ve said
no to everything, spec your next script and

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.430
make it something that you love and knock
it out of the park.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.110
Because she said if the next one is amazing,
that puts you on a trajectory, then people

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.360
see you a certain way.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.670
Later on is the time to do it for money.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.370
Later on we’ll grabble on for the money.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.450
But not for this next script.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.840
Now everyone knows who you are, the next script
is going to tell them what kind of writer

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.170
you are.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:35.670
And when she said that, I had that chill up
my spine that this is absolutely true, I need

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.850
to hear this and do this.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.550
And I said no to something, I said no to something.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:47.790
The third time I said no was a Disney project
and they doubled my quote and I said no.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.340
And they doubled my quote and I said yes.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:54.040
And I’m embarrassed to say that that project
of all the projects was not only a script

00:02:54.040 --> 00:03:00.130
I did not want to write, it was a movie I
wouldn’t even want to see.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:01.520
I don’t come from money.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:09.480
I had student debt and it was more money than
I ever thought you could make in years and

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.430
I was going to get paid for three months.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:19.900
And so the precedent that I set (at least
for myself) was I’m in this for the money

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.290
and that really locked me into a career path.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.910
It was I wish I could go back in time.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:32.040
I feel like that was a really big test and
I failed it.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:37.300
Film Courage: I could see where a lot of people
would not blame you and I’m not even sure

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.910
which project you’re referring to (forgive
me).

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:46.180
So you really feel like even the money that
you took, it probably changed many things

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.960
for you because money can do wonderful things
but it can also hurt some things.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.910
Corey Mandell: But here’s the thing, if
I hadn’t taken that project and that project

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.400
never got made.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.500
And as a writing sample I think it was good
but it wasn’t special.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.892
If I had waited and waited and took something
else or even something original and even if

00:04:05.892 --> 00:04:12.940
it was great, I would have made so much money
down the road.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:21.040
So my agent represents me but he also represents
Aaron Sorkin.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.250
I worked non-stop as a studio writer for 11
years.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:27.700
I made a lot more money than I ever thought
I could make.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.480
Do you know the difference between how much
money Aaron Sorkin is making…I don’t know?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:36.960
But I’m sure that whatever Aaron Sorkin
makes is not even in the same zip code of

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.090
what I made.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.490
He also represents J.K.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.490
Rowling.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:46.930
Now I’m not saying that I could have become
Aaron Sorkin or that level or that I could

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:47.930
have been J.K.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:48.930
Rowling.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:49.930
I don’t know.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.870
But what I do know is that the choices I made
prevented that possibility.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:57.950
I was a studio writer and I just started doing
a bunch of action movies, some were action

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:58.970
comedies.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:02.790
Sometimes I thought they were fun, sometimes
I didn’t but I loved the paycheck.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:08.330
And I loved just making the money and the
deal and I never stopped and wrote from my

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.330
heart.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.130
And I’ll tell you one of the main reasons
was I was so fixed-mindset, I was so afraid

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:15.350
of rejection.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.880
I was so afraid that people would say “Oh,
you’re not that good of a writer, you’re

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.070
a fraud.”

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:29.530
Now if I wrote something from my heart, if
I wrote something that exposed me to the material,

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:33.030
now you’re not a good writer and you’re
not even a good person.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.470
Like they could reject me…if they rejected
my material and it was very personal, then

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.250
that would feel like they rejected me as a
person.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.250
And that was too painful.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.980
I was not going to allow that to happen.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.630
My agent was begging me to write something
authentic and from the heart.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:51.420
My wife was begging me, my manager was begging
me, my Golden Retriever was begging me and

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.530
I just wouldn’t.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:57.210
So A) it was short-sighted.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:01.810
First of all, money isn’t everything but
even if money is everything I potentially

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.190
could have made so much money.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:07.930
But more importantly I could have written
stuff that I was in love with.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.340
Look, I could have tried for that career.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:11.840
I could have written authentic stuff.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.110
I could have swung for the fences, I could
have tried for that A-list career and maybe

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:17.700
come up short.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.090
And then backed into the career I had, maybe?

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.040
I don’t know.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:27.180
But I know that the choices I made then, I
was never going to have that career.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.750
I was never going to be creatively fulfilled.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.810
I was never going to be writing the stuff
that I really wanted to be writing.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.180
I was never going to be writing from love.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.310
I was always going to be writing from fear.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.620
I regret that.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:43.520
And so part of the reason I teach is I want
to help writers do it the right way and help

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.520
empower them with the tools.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:49.230
I wish someone had taught me creative integration
up front and some of the stuff.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:56.639
But I hope that I can be an influence on writers
so that they can have the best possible career

00:06:56.639 --> 00:06:59.730
that they are capable of, maybe even a better
one than that.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:03.660
Film Courage: So if you were to take yourself
to lunch, instead of that women [the agent

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:07.370
Barbara] taking you to lunch and it was an
older you speaking to that younger you, would

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:08.560
you have said the exact same thing?

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.490
Corey Mandell: I would have and I would have
said “And look, I’m from the future so

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:13.580
let me tell you.”

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:19.110
And I would have told him all of the terrible
things that would have happened and I honestly

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.500
think that this younger me would have made
the same decision.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:32.320
The reason is he was so fixed-mindset and
with fixed-mindset you are just working from

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:41.230
fear and you just can’t see the truth or
you can’t…and hopefully that is not true,

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.040
hopefully I would have.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.570
But anyway, I’m not confident that I would
have made a different decision.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:52.650
I’m not proud of that but I think that’s
the truth.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:57.479
But I will say, my wife always sees the real
truth.

00:07:57.479 --> 00:08:00.930
And one of the things you says is all the
things that happened in my career is actually

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:02.450
a blessing.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:05.210
It softened me up.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:10.870
It got me out of this fear space and I wouldn’t
be the teacher that I am now had I not made

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.020
those mistakes and gone through that.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.430
And I did make a lot of money, which is nice.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:22.210
So it’s like it had a lot of perks.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.050
But yeah…I wish I could have done it differently.

